{"id": "s064", "excerpt": "[...]\n## Goal\nAdd a new public `httpx.CookieStore` cookie container implementing deterministic, modern cookie rules (RFC 6265-style), usable anywhere `cookies=` is accepted (including `Client`/`AsyncClient`), without changing existing `Cookies` behavior. Work on a new branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` from master, commit, push to origin, then finish with `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`.\n\n[...]\n- Expiry: `Max-Age` wins over `Expires`; `Max-Age<=0` deletes existing and stores nothing; past `Expires` deletes; invalid `Expires` must not prevent storing.\n- Replacement with same (name, domain, path) counts as newly created for ordering/eviction.\n- Send order: longer path first, then older creation first. `store[\"name\"]` raises `httpx.CookieConflict` when multiple cookies match unless domain/path disambiguates.\n[...]\n### Done\n- Recon: repo at `/app` on `master` (b5addb6). Found remote `origin/feature/deterministic-cookie-store` exists at ea812d9 with 2 junk commits (`scratch/cookie-jar-notes.md` only: \"try a different cookie store approach\", \"more notes, not working yet\"). Searched filesystem/git objects — no existing `CookieStore` implementation anywhere. Existing `Cookies` class at `httpx/_models.py` ~line 1079 uses stdlib `http.cookiejar`.\n- Created branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` from master (`git checkout -b feature/deterministic-cookie-store master`).\n- Created `httpx/_cookie_store.py` (heredoc; checked with `python -c \"import ast; ast.parse(...)\"` → SYNTAX_OK): `_Cookie`/`_ParsedCookie` dataclasses; helpers `_canonical_domain`, `_is_ip_address`, `_domain_match`, `_default_path`, `_path_match`, `_parse_http_date`, `_split_set_cookie_header` (regex `r\",(?=\\s*[^;=\\s]+=)\"` protecting `Expires` commas), `_parse_set_cookie`, `_cookie_applies`; full `CookieStore` (limit validation, `_insert`/`_enforce_limits`, extraction, `set_cookie_header` sorting `key=lambda cookie: (-len(cookie.path), cookie.creation)`, all mapping methods). Finished for now (ruff-formatted, mypy errors pending).\n- Patched `httpx/_models.py` (import CookieStore; `Request.__init__` branches `isinstance(cookies, CookieStore)` → `cookies.set_cookie_header(self)`). ruff clean.\n[...]\n- Patched `httpx/_types.py` (`CookieTypes` union now includes `\"CookieStore\"` with `_cookie_store` TYPE_CHECKING import). Patched `httpx/__init__.py` (`from ._cookie_store import *`; added `\"CookieStore\"` to `__all__`). Verified: `python -c \"import httpx; print(httpx.CookieStore)\"` works; `tests/test_exported_members.py` passes.\n- Created `/tmp/verify_cookie_store.py` comprehensive script; iterated fixes (CookieConflict expectation, AsyncClient needs `async with`, don't pass dict to `CookieStore.__init__`). Final run: `ALL OK` — covers limits, mapping, conflict, extraction, host-only, path matching, default path, domain match, Secure, prefix rules, malformed headers, combined headers w/ Expires comma, expiry, replacement ordering, eviction, all update() forms, Client/AsyncClient integration.\n- Lint/tests: `ruff check httpx tests` → All checks passed; `ruff format httpx/_cookie_store.py` → reformatted; `python -m pytest tests/test_exported_members.py tests/models/test_cookies.py tests/client/test_cookies.py tests/client/test_properties.py -q` → 23 passed; full `python -m pytest tests -q` → 4 failed, 1413 passed, 1 skipped.\n[...]\n### Blocked\n- (none currently; note: pushing will be non-fast-forward because `origin/feature/deterministic-cookie-store` has 2 junk commits ahead of master — will need force-push or reconciliation.)\n\n[...]\n- **`bool` rejected by limit validation** (`isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, int)` → TypeError).\n- **Replacement re-inserts with fresh creation counter** (`_insert` pops then assigns new counter).\n- **`set(domain=\"\")`/mapping inputs → `host_only=False`, domain=\"\"** so `_cookie_applies` skips domain check (sent to any host).\n[...]\n4. `git