/callable-instance-isolation` and push to origin (note: remote branch diverges — push may need `--force` or merge; stale remote commits are scratch-only).\n6. Finish with `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`.\n[...]\n## Critical Context\n- Repo: `/app`; Go 1.13 module; origin = `/srv/git/tengo.git`; master = `3cad0da`; no network access to github.com.\n- Remote `origin/feature/callable-instance-isolation` = f8fdf1b (scratch notes only); local branch recreated fresh from master so it diverges.\n- Key symbols: `CompiledFunction{Instructions, NumLocals, NumParameters, VarArgs, SourceMap, Free []*ObjectPtr, runtime}`, `ObjectPtr`, `Compiled{globalIndexes, bytecode, globals, maxAllocs, runtime, lock}`, `callableRuntime{constants, globals, fileSet, mainFunction, maxAllocs, mu, bound}`.\n- VM: `NewVM(bytecode, globals, maxAllocs)`; tail-call detection compares callee identity; globals indexed by int (so cross-script layout mismatch matters).\n[...]\n- Files created/changed in order with checks:\n  1. `callable.go` (created, then rewritten) — checked via `gofmt -w callable.go` and `go build ./...` (first build failed: `fmt` unused, `v.runtime`/`v.runFunction`/`o.runtime` undefined — expected, patched later).\n  2. `vm.go` (patched: Run refactor, runFunction, wrapRunError, runtimeError, OpCall/OpReturn/OpConstant/OpClosure, global/retVal binding) — `gofmt -w vm.go`; later `go test` caught vm.go:220 panic (fixed).\n[...]\n\n## Original Request\nThe user gave no new requirements in these messages (\"No questions from my side yet. Keep going.\"), instructing the assistant to continue the ongoing task: making script-defined functions/closures callable from Go (`CompiledFunction.Call`) with correct per-instance isolation — deep-cloning foreign callables at every instance boundary (Set/Compile/OpCall/clone), preserving cross-global aliasing, and matching in-script semantics (captures, globals, imports, errors) — on the tengo library at `/app` (branch `feature/callable-instance-isolation`).\n\n[...]\n- VM refactor: per-frame `runtime` field; `frameRuntime()`, `filePos()`, `wrapRunError()`, `runFunction()`, `runtimeError()`, `translateGlobal()`, `touchGlobal()`; OpConstant/OpClosure/OpCall use frame context; OpGetGlobal/OpSetGlobal/OpSetSelGlobal translate slots via name-based `slotMap` (`buildSlotMap`) so cross-layout transfers resolve globals by name; OpReturn supports direct-call return (`functionCall`/`retVal`).\n- Fixed a serious regression: an OpCall rewrite accidentally deleted a large opcode block (`unknown opcode: 21/27`); restored `vm.go` from master (`git show master:vm.go > vm.go`) and reapplied all changes carefully. Fixed source-position formatting (per-frame ip, `v.fileSet` fallback) so error stacks match in-script output.\n- `NewVM` now gets its own runtime so direct-VM functions stay callable from Go; `owns()` and `contextFor()` fixed for instance-less (direct VM) runtimes.\n[...]\n- Key semantics to preserve: transfer snapshots captures at transfer time; destination state persists across repeated Go calls; source instance never mutated; aliasing between transferred values preserved (same cloner); globals resolve by name against destination instance even with different slot layouts; each Go-side argument transfer re-snapshots (documents TestTransferredClosureAsArg behavior).\n- Verification harness lives in `/tmp/repro` (module `repro`, imports tengo via replace) with ~30 scenario tests; debug test files (dbg2/dbg3/enum_test/min_mod_test/pre_test/transfer_test/alias_test) were removed.\n- Known intentional limits: direct `NewVM` globals are not rewritten by `bindTouchedGlobals` (caller may reuse globals, e.g. REPL); `Error` wrapping handled in cloner; `acquireForRuntime` returns `o` unchanged when no foreign callable.\n\n### Files Created/Changed & Verification (in order)\n1. `callable.go` (/app) — added `acquireForRuntime`, `isolateFunction` (later removed), removed dead code (`bindForUse`, `bindCallable`, `cloneCallableValue`, `cloneValue`, `containsCallable`), full rewrite to hybrid runtime model, added `codeIndexes`/`slotMap`/`globalIndexes` + `buildSlotMap`, `acquireArgs`, `bindTouchedGlobals`, `withRuntime`, owns/contextFor fixes. Checked after each edit: `gofmt -w callable.go && go build ./... && go test ./...`. Status: finished (all green).\n2. `script.go` (/app) — shared cloner in Compile; `newRuntime(...)` wiring (incl. `globalIndexes`); `acquireForRuntime` at Set boundary. Checked: gofmt + build + test. Finished.\n[...]\n5. `/tmp/repro/edge_test.go` — created (TestErrorParity, TestTailCallFromGo, TestImportInCalledFunction, TestSourceModuleExportCallFromGo, TestTransferredCaptureAndGlobals, TestNestedTransferIsolation, TestReturnedCompositeCallable, TestCloneCallableIsolation, TestGoCallbackReceivesAndCalls); fixed unused var and stdlib imports. Checked: `go test -run ... -v .`. Passes (Import test fixed later).\n6. `/tmp/repro/cb_test.go` — TestCallbackReentry; rewritten twice (test bug: re-running script overwrote `g`). Passes.\n7. `/tmp/repro/imp_test.go` — TestImportInsideGoCalledFn. Passes."}
{"id": "s067", "excerpt": "[...]\n## Goal\nAdd a new public cookie container `httpx.CookieStore` to the httpx repository that implements deterministic, modern cookie behavior (RFC 6265-style rules), usable anywhere `cookies=` is accepted including `Client`/`AsyncClient`, while leaving existing `Cookies` behavior unchanged. Work must be done on a new branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` from master, committed and pushed to origin.\n\n[...]\n- Host-only vs domain cookies (case-insensitive domain-match, sent to subdomains), default path rules, path matching (\"/sub\" matches \"/sub\", \"/sub/x\", not \"/submarine\")\n- `Secure` only over https; `__Secure-`/`__Host-` prefix rules enforced at store time\n- Expiry: `Max-Age` precedence; `Max-Age<=0`/past `Expires` delete existing; invalid `Expires` still stores\n- Replacement with same (name, domain, path) = newly created for ordering; send order: longer path first, then older creation; `store[\"name\"]` raises `httpx.CookieConflict` when ambiguous\n- Public API: mutable mapping + `extract_cookies`, `set_cookie_header`, `set`, `get`, `delete`, `clear`, `update`\n[...]\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Work on branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` from master; commit and push to origin\n- Keep existing cookie behavior unchanged unless `CookieStore` is used\n[...]\n- Agent must issue at least one bash command per response; ending command must be `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` alone\n- Network is unavailable except local git remote `/srv/git/httpx.git`\n\n[...]\n### Done\n- Explored repo (httpx 0.28.1, Python 3.12); found remote branch `origin/feature/deterministic-cookie-store` contains only scratch notes (commits ef3b2a7, ea812d9 \"Rough notes, try 2\" by Sam Patel)\n- Created local branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` from master (b5addb6)\n[...]\n- Full test suite `python -m pytest tests/ -q -k \"not test_redirect_loop and not network\"` → 1410 passed, 1 skipped, 1 failed (pre-existing unrelated: `tests/test_timeouts.py::test_write_timeout[trio]` PytestUnraisableExceptionWarning)\n- Verified edge cases: quoted values with commas, `Expires` combined headers, whitespace robustness, IP hosts, ports, redirects across hosts, explicit Cookie header overwrite\n- Removed stray untracked `test` file; verified `Cookies(CookieStore)` and `Cookies.update(CookieStore)` now work\n[...]\n- [ ] Final re-run of verification + test suite after latest `Cookies()` conversion change\n- [ ] Commit on `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` and push to origin\n\n[...]\n## Key Decisions\n- **Eager limit enforcement on each `_store()` call**: per-domain eviction (oldest `created` first) runs before global eviction; verified invariant holds at each step\n- **Quote-aware set-cookie splitting** (manual scanner instead of regex `,(?=[^;,]*=)`): handles quoted values containing commas and Expires commas; split only when comma is not in quotes and lookahead finds `name=value`\n[...]\n2. Review final `git diff` / `git status` (modified: `httpx/__init__.py`, `httpx/_client.py`, `httpx/_models.py`, `httpx/_types.py`; new: `httpx/_cookie_store.py`)\n3. Commit on `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` (note: remote branch has 2 scratch commits ahead of master, so push may need `git push -f origin feature/deterministic-cookie-store` or integration of those commits)\n4. Push to origin and verify with `git ls-remote origin`\n5. Run `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` (alone, no other commands)\n[...]\n## Critical Context\n- Repo root `/app`; origin = `/srv/git/httpx.git` (bare repo on disk; no network)\n- Remote `origin/feature/deterministic-cookie-store` = ea812d9 (ahead of master b5addb6 by ef3b2a7 + ea812d9 scratch-note commits); local branch started from master → non-fast-forward push likely, consider force push\n- Key file contents: `httpx/_cookie_store.py` (~530 lines) implements all methods; `__all__ = [\"CookieStore\"]`\n[...]\n\n## Original Request\nThe user said they had no