idation, mapping interface, CookieConflict, clear variants, update sources, domain/path/secure/prefix rules, combined headers with quoted commas/Expires commas, Max-Age/Expires deletion, invalid Expires/Max-Age, ordering, eviction, sync+async client persistence, redirects, copy order. `httpx/_cookie_store.py` = 100% coverage; full-suite coverage of modified files (client/models/cookie_store/types/`__init__`) = 100% (TOTAL 1571 stmts, 0 miss, CI enforces `--fail-under=100`).\n- **Typing/lint**: test file made mypy-clean (typed helpers `extract_cookies`/`send_cookie_header`, `typing.cast(typing.Any, ...)` for negative tests, typed mock handlers, explicit return var). Last good state: `mypy httpx tests` success (62 files), `ruff format`/`ruff check` clean.\n[...]\n- Decide whether to handle or accept the stray-comma splitter edge case.\n- Verification tools: `/tmp/verify_cookie_store.py` (spec harness, prints \"ALL OK\"); scratch `/tmp/check_prefix.py`.\n- Repo/environment: `/app` = httpx; `master` commit 2026-02-23 (Ben Beasley); `origin/feature/deterministic-cookie-store` = ea812d9 \"more notes, not working yet\" / ef3b2a7 \"try a different cookie store approach\" (Sam Patel); merge-base b5addb64; **no commits made this session**.\n- CI expectations: `scripts/check` = ruff format --diff + mypy + ruff check over `httpx tests`; `scripts/test` = coverage run -m pytest with `scripts/coverage` enforcing 100%; Python matrix 3.9–3.13.\n- The user's \"Keep going\" is the only current instruction; continue autonomously.\n\n## Additional Focus: State-Changing / Hard-to-Undo Actions\n- All writes were **local working-tree file edits only** in `/app` (no commits, pushes, force-pushes, branch deletions, or history rewrites occurred or were authorized):\n  - Created/patched `httpx/_cookie_store.py` (module written and repeatedly edited).\n[...]\n  - Patched `docs/api.md`, `docs/quickstart.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` (`git diff --stat`: 7 tracked files, +83/−9; new files untracked).\n  - Created scratch files in `/tmp` (`check_prefix.py`); ran read-only git inspection commands.\n- Authorization: only the user's general continuation (\"Keep going\") — no per-action authorization was given; this permission covers continued local work but was not recorded as covering commits, pushes, or other remote/shared-state operations. None of those were performed."}
