{"id": "s084", "excerpt": "[...]\n- Keep public entrypoint (`CanCall`/`Call`) on the existing callable objects.\n- Work on new branch `feature/callable-instance-isolation` from master, commit, push to origin; finish with `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` only.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- New branch `feature/callable-instance-isolation` from master; commit and push to origin when done.\n- Final command must be exactly `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`, not combined with other commands; after it, work stops.\n[...]\n### Done\n- Reconnaissance of repo: identified key files/services: `objects.go` (CompiledFunction ~line 571: `Instructions, NumLocals, NumParameters, VarArgs, SourceMap, Free []*ObjectPtr`; `CanCall()` line 625; `Copy()` line 597 which does NOT copy `Free` elements; `ObjectPtr` ~1287 with `Value *Object`, `Copy()` returns self), `vm.go` (frame{fn, freeVars, ip, basePointer}; VM{constants,stack,sp,globals,fileSet,frames,...}; `NewVM(bytecode, globals, maxAllocs)`; `Run()` wraps error as `fmt.Errorf(\"Runtime Error: %w\\n\\tat %s\", err, filePos)` then unwinds frames appending `\\n\\tat %s`; `OpCall` line 541; `OpClosure` ~747 builds CompiledFunction with Free; `OpReturn` 670; `OpSuspend` ends MainFunction), `script.go` (`Compiled.Run` 206, `RunContext` 215, `Clone` 258 with `clone.globals[idx] = g.Copy()` at 271, `Get` 295, `Set` 333), `compiler.go` (FuncLit→OpClosure when free symbols; MainFunction gets OpSuspend; modules via parent constants), `bytecode.go` (gob Encode/Decode; `fixDecodedObject`), `builtins.go` (`builtinIsCallable` ~287 uses `args[0].CanCall()`), `errors.go`, `symbol_table.go`, `modules.go`, `variable.go`, `parser/source_file.go` (positions).\n- Confirmed remote layout: origin = `/srv/git/tengo.git`; `master` = 3cad0da; remote branch `origin/feature/callable-instance-isolation` exists at f8fdf1b with 2 notes-only commits (`9a50fcd`, `f8fdf1b`) adding only `scratch/callable-notes.md` (\"Rough notes, try 1/2.\")