arrays/maps, module exports, Go callback args) and when returned closures stay callable.\n3. Implement isolation: freeze captures on transfer (adjust `ObjectPtr`/`CompiledFunction.Copy`, ensure `Compiled.Clone`'s `g.Copy()` isolate callables); recursive isolation through `Array`/`Map`/`ImmutableArray`/`ImmutableMap` copies; destination-globals resolution.\n4. Convert `callable_repro_test.go` into proper tests (or replace with tests in `script_test.go`/new file) covering: globals, nested array/map callables, source-module exports, Go-supplied callback args, variadic, recursion, error formatting parity, clone/transfer isolation incl. mutated captures.\n5. Run `gofmt`, then `go test -race -cover ./...` (and `go run ./cmd/tengo -resolve ./testdata/cli/test.tengo` if needed); fix regressions (watch `TestCompiled_Clone`, bytecode tests, `copy()` builtin tests).\n6. Remove temporary repro file; `git add`/commit on `feature/callable-instance-isolation`; reconcile with remote branch and `git push origin feature/callable-instance-isolation` (may need `--force-with-lease` or rebase on the notes commits).\n7. Finish with exactly `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`.\n[...]\n- **Repro evidence** (current broken behavior): `add CanCall=true`, `add.Call ret=<nil> err=<nil>` — `CompiledFunction` has `CanCall()` (objects.go:625) but no working `Call`; silent nil instead of execution.\n- **Key structs/lines**: `CompiledFunction{Instructions, NumLocals, NumParameters, VarArgs, SourceMap, Free []*ObjectPtr}` (~objects.go:571); `ObjectPtr{Value *Object}` (~1287), `Copy()` returns self; VM `frame{fn, freeVars, ip, basePointer}`; `NewVM(bytecode, globals, maxAllocs)`; `script.go Clone` line ~258: `clone.globals[idx] = g.Copy()`; `Compiled.Set` at script.go:333.\n- **Error strings to match**: `\"Runtime Error: not callable: int\\n\\tat test:7:4\\n\\tat test:3:4\\n\\tat test:9:1\"`, `\"Runtime Error: wrong number of arguments: want=2, got=3\"` / variadic `want>=2`, `\"Runtime Error: