solation**: safely transferring `CompiledFunction` values between `Compiled` instances with correct global-variable index remapping, cloning, and lifecycle behavior.\n[...]\n- Re-running a `Compiled` re-initializes its globals (script-defined values reset; `f` becomes undefined).\n- Last action: scratch test of Go callback (`s.Add(\"apply\", ...)`) calling back into a deep in-script frame failed to compile due to script writing `apply :=` (redeclared — `Add` already defines it); the in-script equivalent works (out: 110). The scratch test needs fixing (drop `apply :=` line) to test the Go-callback path.\n\n## Context Needed to Continue\n- Repo at `/app`; branch `feature/callable-instance-isolation`; master commit 3cad0da. Key line refs: vm.go callFunction ~409, OpConstant stack push vm.go:444, MaxFrames check vm.go:957, tail-call optimization vm.go ~940–965 (MaxFrames=2048).\n- `compileUnit` must stay non-zero-sized for pointer identity; same-unit functions skip remapping; zero-size struct caused all instances to share one address (0x96d020) and broke `TestCallable_TransferredGlobalNotFound`, `TestCallable_RemapDifferentGlobalIndexes`, `TestCallable_TransferGlobalsNameNotInDst`.\n[...]\n- Known test-harness limitation: `require.Equal` stack-overflows on cyclic structures — use pointer equality assertions.\n- Pending: fix scratch Go-callback deep-frame test (remove ˋapply :=ˋ from script since s.Add defines it) and validate callback-into-deep-frame scenario; then final full test run and finish via `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`.\n- Every response must include at least one bash tool call."}
{"id": "s087", "excerpt": "[...]\n## Goal\nAdd a new public `httpx.CookieStore` cookie container to HTTPX (in repo at `/app`) that implements deterministic, modern cookie behavior per a detailed spec (limits/eviction, parsing combined `Set-Cookie` headers, domain/path/Secure/prefix/expiry rules, deterministic send order, conflict detection, mutable-mapping API, `update()` accepting all cookie input forms, usable anywhere `cookies=` is accepted). Must keep existing cookie behavior unchanged unless `CookieStore` is used. Work must be done on a new branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` from master, committed and pushed to origin, then finish with `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT`.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Branch must be named `feature/deterministic-cookie-store`, created from master; commit on it and push to origin when done.\n- `CookieStore` must be exported as `httpx.CookieStore`; `max_cookies`/`max_cookies_per_domain` ints or None (non-int → TypeError, negative → ValueError; evict oldest-creation, per-domain limit first, then global).\n[...]\n- `Max-Age` precedence over `Expires`; `Max-Age<=0` deletes; past `Expires` deletes; invalid `Expires` still stores.\n- Replacement with same (name, domain, path) = newly created for ordering/eviction; send order = longer path first, then older creation first; ambiguous name access raises `httpx.CookieConflict`.\n- `update()` accepts `CookieStore`, `httpx.Cookies`, `http.cookiejar.CookieJar`, `dict[str, str]`, `list[tuple[str, str]]`; mapping/list/`set(domain=\"\")` cookies are non-host-only (sent to any host matching by path/scheme).\n[...]\n### Done\n- Explored repo (`/app`), found old remote branch `origin/feature/deterministic-cookie-store` containing only scratch commits `ea812d9` (\"more notes, not working yet\") / `ef3b2a7` (\"try a different cookie store approach\") with `scratch/cookie-jar-notes.md`.\n- Created local branch: `git checkout -b feature/deterministic-cookie-store master`.\n[...]\n- Fixed during iteration: RFC 6265 default path & path matching; `OverflowError` → `float(\"inf\")` for huge Max-Age; reject domains normalizing to empty (`Domain=.`); jar import marks cookies non-host-only; client merge `elif isinstance(cookies, CookieStore)` for mypy; lint fixes (line lengths, `startswith` tuple, import order).\n- Verified: many inline scripts passed (basic mapping, limits/TypeError/ValueError, host-only vs Domain, case-insensitive domain, subdomain send, combined header with comma Expires, invalid Expires still stores, Secure/prefix rules incl. `__Host-`, Max-Age precedence/deletion, past-Expires deletion, replacement ordering, limits eviction order, CookieConflict, all `update()` forms, Client/AsyncClient integration with MockTransport, `Cookies(store)` interop, `Request(cookies=store)`).\n- Test suites: `python -m pytest tests/models/test_cookies.py tests/client/test_cookies.py -q` → 14 passed; full suite `python -m pytest tests/ -q -m \"not network\" -p no:cacheprovider` → 1411 passed, 1 failed (pre-existing `tests/test_timeouts.py::test_write_timeout[trio]` flake), 1 skipped; `tests/test_exported_members.py` passed.\n[...]\n- **Regex split for combined headers** `,\\s*(?=[^;,\\s=]+=)`: avoids breaking on commas inside `Expires=` dates while splitting `a=1, b=2`.\n- **Internal dict keyed by `(name, domain, path)` → `_Cookie` with monotonic `created` counter**: enables deterministic eviction/ordering; replacement re-creates entry with new counter.\n- **Mapping/list/`set(domain=\"\")` cookies stored with `host_only=False`, empty domain**: matches stdlib CookieJar behavior (verified experimentally: sent to any host). Imported jar cookies also non-host-only.\n[...]\n2. `git add` all changes and commit on `feature/deterministic-cookie-store`.\n3. Push to origin: `git push origin feature/deterministic-cookie-store` (remote branch exists with old scratch commits `ea812d9`/`ef3b2a7`; expect divergence — may need `--force` or fetch/merge decision).\n4. Finish with exactly: `echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` (alone, no other commands).\n[...]\n## Critical Context\n- Repo: `/app`; remote origin = `/srv/git/httpx.git`; Python 3.12; httpx 0.28.1 editable install; master HEAD `b5addb6`.\n- Files created/changed in order:\n[...]\n- Pre-existing failures to ignore: network-dependent tests (`httpx.ConnectError: [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution`) and `tests/test_timeouts.py::test_write_timeout[trio]` unraisable-exception flake.\n- Old remote branch holds only `scratch/cookie-jar-notes.md` commits — desired final state replaces them with the real implementation (force-push may be needed).\n- User check-ins (just continue): \"Quick check-in...\", \"Thanks for the progress so far. Keep going.\", \"this should land this week\", \"heading into a meeting... keep going\", \"Back now. Continue with the task.\" Plus repeated notices that responses must be concise and end with exactly one bash tool call.\n[...]\n\n## Original Request\nAn ongoing (multi-turn) task: implement a new `CookieStore` class for the httpx library on branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store` — a deterministic, dict-like (MutableMapping) cookie container supporting modern cookie rules (RFC 6265-style): limits (`max_cookies`, `max_cookies_per_domain`) with validation and eviction, combined/`Set-Cookie` parsing, host-only vs `Domain` matching, path matching, `Secure`/`__Secure-`/`__Host-` prefixes, expiry precedence (`Max-Age` > `Expires`), cookie-conflict handling, `update()` from dict/list/Cookies/CookieJar/CookieStore, integration with `Client`/`AsyncClient` (including redirects), plus docs/tests/CHANGELOG. In this excerpt the user said only: \"No questions from my side yet. Keep going.\"\n[...]\n- Checked existing tests touching `client.cookies` (`tests/client/test_cookies.py`, `tests/client/test_properties.py`) and confirmed `_client.py` patches: constructor/setter preserve `CookieStore` identity, `cookies` property returns `Cookies | CookieStore`, `_merge_cookies` and `_build_redirect_request` handle `CookieStore`.\n- Ran a comprehensive 11-part heredoc verification (limits validation TypeError/ValueError; per-domain-then-global eviction; combined header with Expires comma + empty value + unknown attr; malformed/no-value attrs ignored; host-only vs Domain incl. `badexample.com`; default/attribute path; Secure + prefix rules; expiry precedence/deletion; replacement ordering `b=1; a=2`; `CookieConflict`; update forms with any-host mapping) — \"ALL COMPREHENSIVE CHECKS PASSED\".\n- Confirmed `CookieStore` is a registered `MutableMapping`; inspected `docs/api.md` Cookies section.\n- Created `tests/models/test_cookie_store.py` (38 tests: mapping interface, limits, eviction, replacement, conflict, delete/clear, update forms, combined header, malformed input, host-only/domain matching, paths, Secure/prefixes, expiry, ordering, client + async client integration). All 38 pass repeatedly.\n- Added `## CookieStore` docs section to `docs/api.md` (before `## Cookies`) and a CHANGELOG entry under `### Added`: \"Add `CookieStore`, a deterministic cookie container supporting modern cookie rules.\"\n- Fixed lint: unused `import time` in new test file (`ruff check --fix`), then `ruff format`.\n- Confirmed redirect behavior (cross-origin host-only cookie not leaked; same-origin redirect sends cookie); a script error (`httpx.get` doesn't take `transport`) was the assistant's test bug, retried correctly.\n- Investigated full-suite failure `tests/test_timeouts.py::test_write_timeout`: reproduced on master via `git stash`/`git stash pop` → pre-existing flakiness, not caused by this work.\n[...]\n- Repo: `/app`, branch `feature/deterministic-cookie-store`, base commit b5addb6. Work is NOT yet committed; `git status` shows modified: `docs/api.md`, `httpx/__init__.py`, `httpx/_client.py`, `httpx/_models.py`, `httpx/_types.py`; untracked: `httpx/_cookie_store.py`, `tests/models/test_cookie_store.py`.\n- Key design decisions: limits validated (`TypeError` for non-int, `ValueError` for negative; 0 = store nothing, `None` = unlimited); eviction oldest-first per-domain then globally; replacement counts as newly created; conflicting names raise `httpx.CookieConflict` on `[]`; cookie with `Domain` from non-matching host rejected; manually-set `Cookie` header not overwritten; `Client(cookies=store)` keeps identity (`client.cookies is store`).\n- Verification baseline: `ruff check` + `mypy httpx/` clean; `tests/models/test_cookie_store.py` 38 passed; `pytest tests/models tests/client -m \"not network\"` 1176 passed; full suite has 1 known flaky failure (`tests/test_timeouts.py::test_write_timeout`, fails on master too)."}
